<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::maritime_incident_rate" target="china_ai_chip_rivalry::foreign_customer_exposur" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rising frequency of hostile or hazardous maritime incidents increases transit delays, insurance and freight costs and delivery uncertainty, causing foreign buyers to reduce orders or diversify suppliers away from China-dependent chip vendors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">china_ai_chip_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::maritime_incident_rate" target="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_capital_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A higher frequency of attacks or interdictions on commercial shipping raises insurance and transport costs, disrupts export receipts for regional issuers and prompts non‑resident investors to reduce or withdraw exposures, lowering net cross‑border capital inflows to affected markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::maritime_incident_rate" target="global_oil_market_shift::shipping_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in hostile incidents prompts insurers to apply war-risk surcharges, owners to detask or reroute tankers and crewing firms to restrict sailings in the theatre, directly reducing effective tanker transport capacity available for oil shipments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::maritime_incident_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_supply_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in hostile incidents against commercial and naval shipping in the Gulf/Red Sea forces rerouting, port closures and sharply higher insurance and transit times, directly slowing or reducing sea-borne deliveries of arms, munitions and logistical supplies destined for Ukraine-supporting forces.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
