<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::energy_supply_risk" target="china_ai_chip_rivalry::investor_risk_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Conflict-related disruptions to oil/gas supplies raise production, power and logistics costs for semiconductor fabs and component suppliers, prompting investors to mark up sector risk and reprioritize capital away from AI chip firms exposed to those supply shocks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">china_ai_chip_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::energy_supply_risk" target="global_bond_market_shock::long_term_bond_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened probability of oil/gas delivery disruptions raises expected long‑run inflation and fiscal risk (higher subsidy/deficit risk and precautionary borrowing), which increases sovereign term premia and pushes up long‑dated government bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::energy_supply_risk" target="global_oil_market_shift::diesel_export_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Conflict-driven interruptions to terminals, pipelines, or shipping lifts the probability that scheduled diesel cargoes are cancelled or cannot load, directly lowering short-term cross-border diesel export volumes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::energy_supply_risk" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_stringency" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Conflict-driven disruptions in Middle East energy supplies raise domestic energy prices and political vulnerability in Europe, making governments politically and economically more likely to delay or soften new sanctions on Russia to avoid further energy shocks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
