  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in refinery utilization reduce the risk of refined-fuel shortages and downward pressure on expected future inflation and the term premium, which in turn lowers long-term sovereign bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
