<edge source="global_oil_market_shift::sanctions_enforcement" target="china_ai_chip_rivalry::export_control_prevalenc" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened sanctions enforcement normalizes use of trade-restriction tools and prompts policymakers to expand and tighten export-control lists and licensing regimes targeting dual-use technologies supplied to sanctioned or sanction-evading actors.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">china_ai_chip_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shift::sanctions_enforcement" target="china_ai_chip_rivalry::regulatory_enforcement_p" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Stricter sanctions enforcement reallocates investigative resources and political attention to cross-border compliance, triggering more frequent probes, audits, and legal actions against firms (including AI chip suppliers) for sanctions and export violations.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">china_ai_chip_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shift::sanctions_enforcement" target="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_capital_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Stricter enforcement of oil-related sanctions increases legal and counterparty risk for banks and investors, prompting rapid withdrawal or rerouting of cross-border credit and investment away from targeted jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shift::sanctions_enforcement" target="iran_regional_conflict::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter sanctions enforcement (inspections, interdictions, vessel blacklists) increases naval and coastguard interdiction activity and confrontations with Iranian ships and proxy actors, raising the frequency of hostile maritime incidents.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_oil_market_shift::sanctions_enforcement" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_stringency" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Stricter enforcement actions (e.g., inspections, interdictions, secondary sanctions) reduce circumvention and thereby translate into a de facto increase in the aggregate restrictiveness and reach of sanctions against actors tied to Russian oil.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_oil_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
