<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::long_term_bond_yield" target="china_ai_chip_rivalry::investor_risk_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in long-term sovereign yields raises discount rates and increases debt-service burdens for capital‑intensive Chinese AI‑chip firms, compressing valuations and making investors more sensitive to execution and demand risks, thereby increasing perceived investor risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_ai_chip_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::long_term_bond_yield" target="global_oil_market_shift::refinery_utilization" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rises in long-term government bond yields increase the cost of working-capital and project finance for refiners and raise the discount rate applied to expected margins, causing some refiners to cut runs or delay maintenance turnarounds and thereby lower utilization in the near term.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::long_term_bond_yield" target="iran_regional_conflict::escalation_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in long-term sovereign yields raise debt‑servicing costs for regional states and their proxy networks, forcing near‑term budget cuts to mobilization, sustainment, and large‑scale operations, which reduces pressure toward broader military escalation.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::long_term_bond_yield" target="russia_ukraine_war::leverage_asymmetry" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in long-term sovereign yields increases borrowing and refinancing costs for Western governments and private donors, tightening fiscal space for sustained military and economic support to Ukraine and thereby increasing Russia's relative bargaining leverage.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
