<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::policy_rate_expectation" target="china_ai_chip_rivalry::foreign_customer_exposur" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher expected short‑term policy rates in advanced‑market customers slow corporate and cloud capital expenditures, causing foreign buyers to delay or reduce orders for high‑end AI chips and thus lowering Chinese firms' foreign‑customer exposure.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_ai_chip_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::policy_rate_expectation" target="global_oil_market_shift::diesel_export_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher expected short-term policy rates (especially in the USD area) strengthen the dollar and tighten trade financing conditions, reducing import demand in dollar-priced markets and compressing trade credit lines for exporters, which lowers diesel export flows in the short run.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shift</data>
</edge>
