<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::market_volatility" target="china_ai_chip_rivalry::regulatory_enforcement_p" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in financial‑market volatility increase political and supervisory attention to market stability and sectoral risks, prompting regulators and prosecutors to accelerate investigations, compliance reviews and enforcement actions targeting AI‑chip firms.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_ai_chip_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::market_volatility" target="global_oil_market_shift::diesel_price_spread" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in financial-market volatility raise risk premia and reduce liquidity in refined-product trading, prompting wider bid-ask spreads and forcing holders to demand larger margins on diesel relative to crude, widening the diesel price spread within weeks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::market_volatility" target="iran_regional_conflict::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in financial market volatility drive up war‑risk and hull insurance premiums and prompt private security contractors and insurers to scale back operations in high‑risk waterways, leaving vessels more exposed and raising the frequency of hostile incidents and accidents.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::market_volatility" target="russia_ukraine_war::coalition_consensus" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp financial-market volatility that imposes asymmetric economic pain on coalition members (currency moves, market losses, banking stress) elevates domestic priorities and political divisions, weakening agreement within multilateral coalitions on coordinated policy toward Russia.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
