<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_capital_flo" target="china_ai_chip_rivalry::export_control_prevalenc" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained net capital outflows from China raise strategic and national‑security concerns among importing‑country policymakers, motivating them to expand the scope and strictness of export controls on advanced semiconductors.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_ai_chip_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_capital_flo" target="global_oil_market_shift::shipping_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Increases in cross-border capital inflows lower financing costs and improve access to leasing/refinance for tanker owners and operators, enabling more charters, fewer vessel layups and timely acceptance of newbuilds, which raises effective shipping capacity over the medium term.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_capital_flo" target="iran_regional_conflict::energy_supply_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp net capital outflows from Gulf markets quickly tighten bank liquidity and curtail trade‑finance and pre‑export lending that underpins oil shipments and tanker operations, increasing the probability of short‑term energy delivery disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_capital_flo" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_supply_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Increases in cross-border capital flows ease financing for arms procurement, export credit and donor transfers, accelerating payment, contracting and deliveries of military equipment and munitions to forces supporting Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
